# - Review first: Table 1 is read in column order SchNet (energy RMSE, MAE; force RMSE, MAE) then PaiNN (same). Energies are total-energy errors of 56-atom (54-atom for clean slabs) cells in meV, not per atom. The settings (7 interactions, 512 features, 4 A cutoff, loss weights 0.05 / 0.95) are the optimised ones the paper states for the final models; whether the 'initial model' rows of Table 1 use the same settings on the initial data, as the table suggests, is assumed. The models used during adaptive sampling were SchNet with default settings, a 5 A cutoff and batch size 10 and are not encoded.
# - PaiNN was run through SchNetPack, so its implementation points at the vocabulary library SchNet (meaning the SchNetPack code base) with the version string naming the branch.
# - Errors are averages over 5 models with different random train/test splits; one run per method and data set is encoded. Sticking probabilities against experiment, minimum-energy paths, elbow plots and learning curves are not encoded.
# - Read from the arXiv v5 preprint; arXiv id matched by title and author.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

